---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About Archytum" description="An Azure architecture and AI engineering consultancy built around evidence, control, and right-sized delivery.">
  <PageHero eyebrow="About Archytum" title="Practical systems. Sound judgment. Clear control." lede="Archytum exists to help organizations use Azure and AI as operating capabilities—not as disconnected demonstrations or invisible automation." />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container grid-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Purpose</p>
        <h2>Build the right-sized system.</h2>
        <p>Archytum helps organizations turn cloud, AI, integration, and business-automation needs into bounded systems with clear ownership and measurable acceptance criteria.</p>
        <p>The work begins with the operating problem, the decision that must improve, and the controls the organization must preserve.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
        <h2>Evidence before expansion.</h2>
        <p>Architecture and automation should create a visible operating result without hiding risk or authority. Scope, permissions, cost, and complexity expand only when evidence supports the next step.</p>
        <p>Capabilities and examples are published only when their status, source, limitations, and approval are clear.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">The standard</p><h2>What clients should expect.</h2></div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Plain decisions</h3><p>Tradeoffs, assumptions, owners, and acceptance criteria are written down—not hidden behind jargon.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Controlled access</h3><p>Read and write permissions remain separate. Access expands only when it is justified and approved.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Honest evidence</h3><p>Demonstrations, recommendations, and measured results are labeled accurately. Unknowns remain visible.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="narrow content" style="padding:0">
      <h2>Responsible automation is an operating design.</h2>
      <p>Human approval is placed immediately before consequential actions. Email, calendar descriptions, documents, websites, and retrieved content are treated as untrusted input. Customer data is minimized, isolated, and never used to train an Archytum-owned model.</p>
      <blockquote>Automation earns authority through evidence. It does not receive authority because the technology is impressive.</blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>
